CROSS-PLATFORM AGREEMENT (the reason both transcripts are kept)

Both platforms landed THE SAME 15 files with [oracle OK] on every one, and both
refused the shortfall arm having written nothing. The two runs disagree on
nothing that matters and agree on the file set, which is the claim the spec
exists to defend.

Windows measures recorded here for the first time:
  hydrate   27 file(s), 104411 B, 68.8906 ms (zero disk reads)
  writeback 15 file(s),  95579 B, 57.4753 ms
  manifest  13 table(s) declared, all present
  indexes   12 selection(s) travel in the posture, files NOT written

The 27-vs-15 gap is the documented index behavior, not a shortfall: hydration
carries 13 tables + 12 index containers + 2 memo sidecars out of the memo, while
writeback lands 13 tables + 2 sidecars because index FILES are derived and
rebuildable at the destination -- the CHOICE travels in the posture. `WITH
INDEXES` is the byte-mirror option and remains UNTESTED.

Teardown removed 16 entries, so the run left nothing behind.
